d_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\r\n\r\n- Reproducible in 4.1.1-stable, 4.3-stable and 4.4-dev4\r\n\r\n### System information\r\n\r\nGodot v4.3.stable - Windows 10.0.19045 - Vulkan (Forward+) - integrated Intel(R) UHD Graphics (Intel Corporation; 31.0.101.2114) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-10510U CPU @ 1.80GHz (8 Threads)\r\n\r\n### Issue description\r\n\r\nAfter pressing any keyboard button, even ones that are not bound to actions, GUI Buttons cannot be pressed and remain inactive for about another second. \r\nThis may be intended behavior, but I found nothing in the documentation to indicate it.\r\nModifier keys such as shift work fine.\r\nMouse enter events work as well.\r\nTried to set it to the right mouse button but got the same result.\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n- Create a new project\r\n- Add a Button.\r\n- Connect the pressed signal to a function that prints a message\r\n- Start the project\r\n- Press a button, such as a number (Modifier keys such as Shift do not produce this behavior)\r\n- Try pressing the button\r\n- The function will not be called while the button is pressed, or for some time after.\r\n\r\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\r\n\r\n[GUIButtonTest.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/17744137/GUIButtonTest.zip)\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"3l3m01","id":15616146,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NjE2MTQ2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15616146?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/3l3m01","html_url":"https://github.com/3l3m01","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/3l3m01/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/3l3m01/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/3l3m01/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/3l3m01/st